"""Beginner advice and dated official-source free entry points."""
def publish_beginner_pages(page, cfg):
    page('/start/', 'Start using AI: your first useful task | '+cfg['brand'], 'Write a brief, check an AI draft and keep actions under your control.', '''
<section class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">START HERE</p><h1>Your first useful AI task</h1><p class="lede">Turn a small set of notes into a draft, compare it with your input, then save and reopen it in the editor you will actually use. Finish with a checked, usable file.</p></section><article class="prose">
<h2>Choose a task with a clear finish</h2><p>Try reorganising your own notes, outlining an article or drafting a routine message. Write down what a useful result looks like before opening a tool. Work on a copy and remove private identifiers. For a first exercise, avoid payments, account changes and decisions you cannot independently verify.</p>
<h2>Give a brief, not just a topic</h2><p>Specify the audience, input, output and limits. Ask the assistant to identify missing information rather than invent facts.</p><blockquote>Turn the notes below into a short project update for a colleague. Use only facts in the notes. Separate completed work, blockers and next steps. If a date or owner is missing, mark it unknown. Do not send the message.</blockquote><p>Use the prompt as a starting point and replace the notes with your own.</p>
<h2>Check the draft against the input</h2><ol><li>Compare names, dates, numbers and promises with your original notes.</li><li>Remove unsupported additions. Open cited sources and check that they support the claims.</li><li>Request one specific correction, such as separating a proposed deadline from an agreed deadline.</li><li>Review the final version yourself before sending or publishing it.</li></ol>
<h2>Save the file and try an edit</h2><p>Do not stop at the chat preview. Save a small sample in your intended editor, reopen it independently and change one value. Save and reopen again to confirm the change persisted. For a table, compare each value with its row label; for a message, check names, dates and missing details.</p><p>For practice, use an invented refund of -3.50 USD and an owner marked UNKNOWN. Check that the saved file keeps the minus sign and leaves the owner unknown. Correct any change and keep the original notes beside the file.</p><figure class="editorial-figure"><img src="/assets/editorial/ai-export-check.svg" width="760" height="600" alt="Define a destination, export a sample, reopen and edit, then compare with the original input."/><figcaption>Finish the task in the file you will use.</figcaption></figure><p><a href="/ai-tools/check-free-ai-export/">Try the full export exercise and checklist</a>.</p><h2>Keep actions under your control</h2><p>A chatbot drafts text; an agent may also use tools and change files or accounts. Check the permissions, which destination receives your data, and whether an action can be undone. Approve concrete actions after reviewing the result. Never include passwords or identity documents in a public example.</p>
<h2>Decide whether you need a paid plan</h2><p>Test a free entry point on representative work first. Record which limit blocks completion: input size, usage, export or integration. Evaluate a paid plan when it solves that specific limit. Paying does not remove the need to check the output.</p>
<h2>Keep a practice record</h2><p>Record the task, non-sensitive input, tool and version if shown, corrections and final result. Include failures and manual work. That record will help you spot the same problem next time.</p><p><a href="/free-ai/">Free entry points</a> · <a href="/ai-tools/meta-muse-guide/">Muse beginner guide</a> · <a href="/ai-tools/verify-ai-meeting-summaries/">Verify a meeting summary</a></p><p>The prompts and practice notes are examples, not results from a product test.</p></article>''', lastmod='2026-10-07')
    page('/free-ai/', 'Free AI tools: choose a task, check the limits | '+cfg['brand'], 'Official-source free AI plans with dated checks and clearly stated limits.', '''
<section class="page-hero task-hero"><p class="eyebrow">FREE AI TOOLS</p><h1>Start with a task.<br><span>Check what is free.</span></h1><p class="lede">For coding, compare Copilot Free and Cursor Hobby below. For documents, prepare readable text and verify the answer. A free app does not make every model or API free.</p><div class="task-links"><a href="#free-plans">Compare free coding plans</a><a href="/ai-tools/scanned-pdf-to-text/">Prepare a document for AI</a><a href="/start/">Draft your first useful result</a><a href="#limit-recovery">Recover an unfinished task</a></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="grid task-grid"><article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">WRITE &amp; CHECK</p><h2><a href="/start/">Turn notes into a draft</a></h2><p>Specify the facts, audience and missing details. Check the answer against your own notes.</p></article><article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">CODE &amp; REVIEW</p><h2><a href="#free-plans">Make one small change</a></h2><p>Compare current free coding plans. Keep the original code and verify the final change.</p></article><article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">READ &amp; VERIFY</p><h2><a href="/ai-tools/scanned-pdf-to-text/">Get usable document text</a></h2><p>Check whether you need OCR, preserve page labels and compare numbers with the original.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="prose"><figure class="editorial-figure"><img src="/assets/editorial/free-ai-task-check.svg" width="760" height="587" alt="Four checks for a free AI task: define the result, check access type, identify the stopping limit, and verify the saved result."/><figcaption>Four checks before choosing a free tool.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Can you keep editing the result?</h2><p>Check a saved file before building your workflow around a free plan. Our <a href="/ai-tools/check-free-ai-export/">export exercise</a> includes practice notes and the values to look for.</p></section><section class="section" id="limit-recovery"><h2>Free limit reached? Keep your progress first.</h2><p>Record the exact blocked step and any reset time shown by your account. Save your original input, checked facts, unfinished draft and the next step in a file. Leave missing details as UNKNOWN.</p><ol><li>Copy relevant source material with labels, such as S1 for capacity and S2 for bookings.</li><li>Separate checked facts from suggested wording. Retain the draft, but mark unsupported dates, owners and counts.</li><li>Reopen the saved notes and compare them with the originals. Resume one small step when access is available.</li></ol><p>Our Cedar practice case uses 8 seats, 6 confirmed participants and 3 people waiting. The remaining 2 seats are derived from capacity minus confirmed bookings; the waiting list stays separate. <a href="/ai-tools/save-free-ai-progress/">Use the save-and-resume template and worked example</a>.</p><figure class="editorial-figure"><img src="/assets/editorial/ai-quota-handoff.svg" width="760" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Save input, checked facts, unfinished draft and one next action in your own file."/><figcaption>You can save these notes without sending another prompt.</figcaption></figure></section><section class="section" id="free-plans"><h2>Free coding plans with official sources</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Tool / plan</th><th>Access type</th><th>Limits to check</th><th>Source / reviewed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><a href="/ai-tools/github-copilot/">GitHub Copilot Free</a></td><td>Free AI coding plan</td><td>Limited chat and agent usage. Feature access differs from paid plans; check your editor and eligibility.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/features/copilot/plans" rel="noopener">Official plan comparison</a><br>Listed as available<br>Reviewed 2026-10-04</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/ai-tools/cursor/">Cursor Hobby</a></td><td>Free entry plan for the Cursor editor</td><td>The current Hobby page lists limited Agent requests, Composer access and no credit card required. A model-provider API is a separate service.</td><td><a href="https://cursor.com/pricing" rel="noopener">Official pricing</a><br>Listed as available<br>Reviewed 2026-10-04</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section><article class="prose"><h2>Read the conditions first</h2><p>A free plan, a timed trial, promotional credits and downloadable model weights are different things. Check region eligibility, payment-method requirements, renewal behaviour, data handling and the limit relevant to your task. Use the official plan page and signup screen to check those conditions.</p><h2>Questions before you start</h2><details><summary>Is a free plan the same as a trial?</summary><p>No. A continuing free tier and access that ends after a stated time have different stopping points. Check the end date, export conditions and renewal behaviour on the official page.</p></details><details><summary>What if I hit a free limit?</summary><p>Save your original input, checked facts, unfinished draft and one next action in your own file. Record the exact limit notice; a new chat does not guarantee a restored allowance. <a href="#limit-recovery">Follow the recovery steps above</a>.</p></details><details><summary>Can I trust an AI summary of a scan immediately?</summary><p>First compare the extracted text with the page image. Check numbers, units and row headings before using the summary.</p></details><h2>Updates and history</h2><p>The dates above show when we reviewed the sources. Check the official page and your account for later changes. If a source cannot be checked, we mark it unverified rather than assuming the plan has ended.</p><p>The plan links above are direct official links, not affiliate links.</p><p><a href="/start/">Start with one useful task</a> · <a href="/ai-tools/coding-assistant-checklist/">Choose a coding assistant</a> · <a href="/offers/">Verified offers</a></p></article>''', lastmod='2026-10-07')
